      "en": "Trust in facts comes not from one side's authority but from a transparent path between a claim, its source, and verification. Research on war should identify in advance what a document actually proves, how close it is to the event, whether independent corroboration exists, and which alternative explanations remain. This standard does not require absolute completeness before any conclusion; it requires matching the strength of language to the quality of evidence and revising the picture when better information appears.",
